# msgpack (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964) and setuptools (CVE-2025-47273) are flagged by Trivy
# at versions 1.1.2 / 70.3.0, but those versions come from pip's own internal
# vendor.txt manifest (/opt/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt),
# which just records which versions pip vendors for its own bundled/internal use. This
# is not an installed application package and is not reachable via this connector's
# code or any untrusted external input.
#
# Verified 2026-09-16 in the built image:
#   pip show msgpack     -> Package(s) not found
#   pip show setuptools  -> Package(s) not found
# (same pip==26.1.1 vendor.txt as the database-connector fix, issue #2439)
#
# Re-evaluate if pip itself bumps its vendored copies to fixed versions, or if a
# future finding shows a real installed-package occurrence (not pip/_vendor).
